// REPRODUCED (semantics-v2-subtype-rules, ruling 2026-10-10). [CR#704.5m] is
// the state-based action "if this Aura is not attached, put it into its owner's
// graveyard". Its other half, "attached to an illegal object or player", is NOT
// written: legality is the engine's attach-permission model under default-deny
// (the Enchant keyword's "may be attached to [quality]" [CR#702.5a,303.4c]), and
// the condition reads the attachment relation that model keeps. No
// `legallyAttached` primitive is written.
//
// The v1 core type-rule record this declaration carried until
// `plugins-v2-subtypes-macro-only`, preserved verbatim so nothing is lost:
//
//     body: Subtype(
//         name: "Aura",
//         types: [Enchantment],
//         confers: [
//             StateBased(
//                 condition: Not(LegallyAttached(This)),
//                 effect: Move(This, Graveyard),
//             ),
//         ],
//     ),
//
// Aura ([CR#205.3h]) — an enchantment subtype whose type rule ([CR#303.4c])
// puts it into its owner's graveyard as a state-based action ([CR#704.5m]).
// That is a [CR#704] game action, not an ability of any kind: [CR#704.1]
// state-based actions "happen automatically" and "don't use the stack", and
// [CR#704.1a] reserves the ability hierarchy for things that WATCH state
// (triggered abilities). So the conferral is the ability-free
// `StateBased(condition, effect)` flavor, never an `Ability` of any kind
// ([CR#604.1] static abilities "do something all the time").
//
// The targeting + legal-host + enters-attached parts are the Enchant KEYWORD's
// ([CR#702.5a]) — a genuine static ability — and stay off this declaration.
Subtype(
    category: Enchantment,
    name: "aura",
    spelling: "Aura",
    grammar: Noun(singular: "Aura"),
    params: [],
    rules: [
        StateBased(
            not(matches(thisAura, attachment(Attachment))),
            move(thisAura, battlefield, graveyard),
        ),
    ],
)
